<%# FUIME: for whoever actions COPPA requests at Fuime. Leads with the deadline
    because that is the part with legal weight. %>

<p>
  <strong><%= @requester.name || @requester.email %></strong> has asked Fuime to
  delete the account of
  <strong><%= @subject_user.name || @subject_user.email %></strong>.
</p>

<table>
  <tr><td>Requested</td><td><%= @data_request.requested_at.strftime("%B %-d, %Y") %></td></tr>
  <tr><td>Reply by</td><td><%= @data_request.due_at.strftime("%B %-d, %Y") %></td></tr>
  <tr><td>Reason given</td><td><%= @data_request.reason.presence || "—" %></td></tr>
</table>

<p>
  Check for open disputes and unsettled payouts first —
  <code>Fuime::DataErasureService#blockers</code> lists them, and both are
  reasons to reply with a date rather than to refuse. Then:
</p>

<pre>rake fuime:data_request:fulfil[<%= @data_request.id %>]</pre>

<p>
  This severs the person from Fuime's records; it does not destroy the sales
  ledger, which is Fuime's own accounting record as merchant of record. That is
  what the parent was told on the page they clicked.
</p>

<p><%= link_to "All data requests", @admin_url %></p>
